#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119808 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119619 :question/id #uuid "d5a81b39-421e-55c3-90de-d9f4e6489cd5" :question/math-academy-id "e-4795" :question/problem "Determine if $\\mathbf{b}$ lies in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\},$ where\n$$\n\\mathbf{a_1}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{a_2}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{array} \\right]}, \\qquad\n\t\\mathbf{b}={\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ - 5\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We know that $\\mathbf{b} \\in \\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}$ if there exist $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}} & =\\mathbf{b} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2} &=8 \\\\ {x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nTo solve the system above, we set up and row reduce an augmented matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -5\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -8 & -21\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+8{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe third row of the augmented matrix now corresponds to the equation $0x_1 + 0x_2 = 3,$ which has no solution.\n\nSo, there are no values of $x_1$ and $x_2$ such that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{1}}+{x}_{2}{\\mathbf{a}}_{\\mathbf{2}} & =\\mathbf{b} \\\\ {x}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+{x}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $\\mathbf{b}$ does *not* lie in $\\textrm{Span}\\{ \\mathbf{a_1}, \\mathbf{a_2} \\}.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "aaefbc53-9df9-54a0-a969-66e062553d5c" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048445 :topic/difficulty 0.796474225322724 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428325 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account differential: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: differential=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/differential-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1733->1049. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048742} :encompassing/weight 1.0} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428326 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account differential: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; 